Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "UnrealisticAnimalCrossing" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2, :actor3 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Elephant crossing road from right" .
:actor2 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Elephant crossing road from left" .
:actor3 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Elephant walking on road" .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Unrealistic animal presence in roadway" .

:weather1 a :ClearCondition ;
    :description "Clear weather, daytime" .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Elephant crossing road in front of vehicle" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :LaneIntrusionRisk ;
    :description "Animals occupying multiple lanes" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :DistractionRisk ;
    :description "Unusual scene may distract driver" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.95"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.88"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

